            <ArticleTitle>Serial coronary arteriography with 105mm photofluorography: 24-month experience, 2,200 patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>421-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 105 mm camera has been used for over 24 mo in evaluation of the coronary circulation for the most part and occasionally the proximal peripheral arteries in 2,200 patients. This photofluorographic technique provides sufficient diagnostic image detail with improved operating convenience and reduced radiation exposure compared to the large film changer. 105 mm serialography is a good adjunct to cine arteriography as a complementary film recording system, and in many cases may supplement large film serialography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
